---
name: "Partners"
title: "Partner for genetic screening in India | Lightening Lives"
description: "Hospitals, diagnostic labs, public health programmes and NGOs partner with us for genetic screening. Our partners include CSIR-CCMB and Tata Trusts."
label: Partners
h1: 'Partner with us. <span class="h-mark">Choose how we work together.</span>'
lead: "Laboratories, health programmes and foundations work with us to bring confirmed genetic diagnosis to the people who need it."
proof:
  - { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" }
  - { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" }
  - { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
notice: true
closing:
  h2: 'Tell us about your laboratory, <span class="h-mark">programme or community.</span>'
  body: "Tell us the condition you need to test for and where the testing will happen. We will take it from there."
  solid: { text: "Start a conversation", href: "/contact/" }
  line: { text: "How the test works", href: "/technology/" }
---
{#- Partners (content file 5.6; one page since 25 October 2026, the reviewer's site map, 3.1). Where
    every "Partner with us" button leads. The three doors stand above the fold and lead to the three
    sections written for each reader (5.6.1 to 5.6.3, confirmed lines only: a [CONFIRM] there is left
    out, never shown); then who we already work with, and how a partnership starts. It replaces
    /partnerships/ and /programmes/, which forward here (src/site/_data/forwards.json). The bands run
    mist (the opening and its doors), then paper and stone in turn, to the sprout close. -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' %}
{%- from "doors.njk" import doorList with context %}
{%- from "model.njk" import testingModel %}
{%- from "faq.njk" import faq %}

  <!-- 1. The three ways to partner, under the opening, on its ice white -->
  <section id="start" class="section on-mist partner-start" aria-label="Three ways to partner">
    <div class="wrap">
      {{ doorList(true) }}
      <p class="doors-else">{% icon "message-circle" %}<span>Something else? Research, a new test or the media: <a class="link" {{ { who: "other" } | enquire | safe }}>talk to us {{ arrow | safe }}</a></span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. For hospitals and laboratories -->
  <section id="laboratories" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="laboratories-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="laboratories-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">For hospitals and laboratories. <span class="h-mark">Confirmed diagnosis, in your own laboratory.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Run screening and confirmation in one test, on a dried blood spot, with the PCR equipment you already have.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="audience mt-12">
        <div>
          <h3 class="audience-h">What changes for your laboratory</h3>
          <ul class="ticks mt-5">
            <li>{% icon "flask-conical" %}<p><strong>No DNA extraction.</strong> A punch from the card goes straight into the reaction.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "thermometer" %}<p><strong>Samples arrive at room temperature.</strong> Dried cards need no cold chain.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<p><strong>One test instead of two.</strong> Screening and confirmation in a single run.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "layers" %}<p><strong>High throughput.</strong> Many cards in one run.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "stethoscope" %}<p><strong>Results your clinicians can act on.</strong> Patient, carrier or unaffected.</p></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="audience-card" aria-labelledby="lab-needs-h">
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "microscope" %}</span>
          <h3 id="lab-needs-h" class="audience-h">What your laboratory needs</h3>
          <p>A thermal cycler, a gel tank and a punch, and staff who have run PCR or have been trained. We help set the method up.</p>
          <a class="link" href="/technology/#laboratory">The full list {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <h3 class="audience-h mt-12">How we work with you</h3>
      <ol class="flow mt-5">
        <li><span class="flow-n">1</span><p><strong>A conversation</strong> with our scientific team about the conditions you test for.</p></li>
        <li><span class="flow-n">2</span><p><strong>Training for your staff,</strong> and help setting the method up.</p></li>
        <li><span class="flow-n">3</span><p><strong>Supply and ongoing support</strong> as your laboratory runs the tests.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="audience-act">
        <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "laboratory" } | enquire | safe }}>Talk to our scientific team</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. For public health programmes -->
  <section id="programmes" class="section" aria-labelledby="programmes-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="programmes-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">For public health programmes. <span class="h-mark">Screen and confirm in one visit.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">For district, state and national programmes: one finger-prick sample, room-temperature transport, a confirmed result, and newborns tested at birth.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="answers mt-12">
        <li>
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "user-x" %}</span>
          <p><strong>People lost between screening and confirmation.</strong> One test screens and confirms, so no one waits for a second visit.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "snowflake" %}</span>
          <p><strong>A cold chain from village to laboratory.</strong> Dried cards travel at room temperature, by ordinary courier or post.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "baby" %}</span>
          <p><strong>Newborns who leave before testing.</strong> A newborn can be tested at birth.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="audience-h mt-12">How a programme runs</h3>
      {{ testingModel("mt-5") }}
      <div class="audience-foot mt-12">
        {%- set names = [] %}{% for st in work.states %}{% set names = (names.push(st.name), names) %}{% endfor %}
        <p class="audience-where">{% icon "map-pin" %}<span>Population and newborn screening at 15 sites in nine states and Delhi: {{ names.slice(0, -1).join(", ") }} and {{ names | last }}.</span></p>
        <div class="audience-act">
          <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "programme" } | enquire | safe }}>Plan a programme</a>
          <a class="link" href="/our-work/">Our work {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. For CSR and NGOs -->
  <section id="funders" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="funders-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="funders-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">For CSR and NGOs. <span class="h-mark">Fund screening that ends in a diagnosis, not a referral.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Your support reaches a confirmed result, counselling and follow-up for every family.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="audience mt-12">
        <div>
          <h3 class="audience-h">Why it matters</h3>
          <ul class="ticks mt-5">
            <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<p><strong>Each rupee reaches an answer.</strong> Screening that stops at a possible case helps no one; one test that confirms does.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "megaphone" %}<p><strong>A camp both explains and tests.</strong> Community screening and awareness camps are run together.</p></li>
            <li>{% icon "heart-handshake" %}<p><strong>Families are not left alone with a result.</strong> Every family a programme finds is counselled and supported.</p></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-faq">
          <h3 class="audience-h">Questions funders ask</h3>
          {{ faq([
            { q: "We are an NGO with no laboratory. Can we still run screening?", a: "Yes. Cards travel at room temperature to a nearby testing centre, so the laboratory need not be yours. Tell us where you plan to screen and we will say how the samples would be tested." },
            { q: "Do you work with CSR funders?", a: "Yes. Most population-level screening is funded that way or by government. Tell us the community and the condition, and we will propose a programme." },
            { q: "What happens to the families a programme identifies?", a: "Counselling for patients and carriers, a path to treatment where it exists, and support groups. That is part of the programme, not an extra." }
          ]) }}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="audience-act">
        <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "funder" } | enquire | safe }}>Fund a programme</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Who we already work with: the logos, in their groups -->
  <section id="partners" class="section" aria-labelledby="partners-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="partners-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">We work with <span class="h-mark">institutions, foundations and patient groups.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Thirteen organisations so far, in three groups.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="logo-groups is-stacked mt-12">
        {%- for key, label in partners.groups %}
        {%- set group = partners.logos | where("group", key) | where("published", true) %}
        {%- if group.length %}
        <div class="logo-group" style="--n: {{ group.length }}">
          <h3 class="logo-group-h">{{ label }}</h3>
          <ul class="logo-row">
            {%- for p in group %}
            <li><img src="/assets/logo/partners/{{ p.file }}" width="{{ p.width }}" height="{{ p.height }}" alt="{{ p.name }}" style="--ratio: {{ (p.width / p.height) | round(3) }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. How a partnership starts: four steps -->
  <section id="how-it-starts" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="how-it-starts-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="how-it-starts-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">How a partnership starts. <span class="h-mark">Four steps, from the first conversation.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">You bring the condition you need to screen for or diagnose. We bring the test, the method, the training and the counselling that follows a result.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="start-steps mt-12">
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "message-circle" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">1</span> You tell us the need</h3><p>The condition and the setting: who will be tested, roughly how many, where samples will be collected and which laboratory will run them.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "clipboard-list" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">2</span> We agree the scope</h3><p>What the test must detect, how results will be reported, and what training and counselling the programme needs.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "dna" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">3</span> We develop or adapt the test</h3><p>A test we have, or a new one for the mutations your population carries.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "graduation-cap" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">4</span> We train and stay with you</h3><p>Through reporting, counselling and follow-up.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
